      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "The edge length of a square can be expressed in two different ways, so we can set these two expressions equal to each other and solve for $x$:\n\\begin{align*}\n4x - 15 &= 20 - 3x \\\\\n4x + 3x &= 20 + 15 \\\\\n7x &= 35 \\\\\nx &= 5\n\\end{align*}\nNow that we know the value of $x$, we can substitute it into either expression to find the length of an edge of the square:\n\\begin{align*}\n4(5) - 15 &= 20 - 3(5) \\\\\n20 - 15 &= 20 - 15 \\\\\n5 &= 5\n\\end{align*}\nSince both expressions are equal to 5, we can conclude that the length of an edge of the square is 5 meters.\nThe area of a square is equal to the length of an edge squared, so the area of this square is $5^2 = \\boxed{25}$ square meters.",
