    "text": "The edge of the square is given by two expressions: $4x-15$ meters and $20-3x$ meters. Since both expressions represent the same edge, we can set them equal to each other and solve for $x$:\n\n\\begin{align*}\n4x-15 &= 20-3x \\\\\n7x &= 35 \\\\\nx &= 5\n\\end{align*}\n\nNow that we have the value of $x$, we can substitute it back into either expression to find the length of the edge of the square:\n\n\\begin{align*}\n4x-15 &= 4(5)-15 \\\\\n&= 20-15 \\\\\n&= 5 \\text{ meters}\n\\end{align*}\n\nThe area of a square is given by the square of its side length. Therefore, the area of the square is:\n\n\\begin{align*}\n\\text{Area} &= 5^2 \\\\\n&= 25 \\text{ square meters}\n\\end{align*}\n\nSo, the area of the square is $\\boxed{25}$ square meters.",
